{"base_rate":0.40290620871862615,"brier":0.19645495376486127,"bss":0.18338666183084296,"bss_hi":0.2838011053400608,"bss_lo":0.07082654518635219,"chart":{"base":[410.3,195.8],"fp":[367.8,159.1],"lead":"62,278.4 272,250.6 482,208.6 692,141.8","note":{"base":"skill 0.18 — higher than 26% of cities","fp":"low end +10pp, high end +24pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.8 °C — better than 88% of cities","rel":"promised 2% → rained 11%; promised 94% → rained 70%"},"rel":"74.1,416.4 291.5,303.7 652.7,164.7"},"country":"FI","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.1536063408190224,"ess":428.68827908707857,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Turku</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Turku rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (98%), believe about\n<b>73%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>8%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 757 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nTURKU ARTUKAINEN, 4.8 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.18, ranked 160 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(109&ndash;182) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>8%</b></td><td class='num'>225</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>7%</td><td class='num'><b>23%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>23%</td><td class='num'><b>33%</b></td><td class='num'>81</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>51%</td><td class='num'><b>42%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>77%</td><td class='num'><b>57%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>98%</td><td class='num'><b>73%</b></td><td class='num'>236</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Turku</b> <span class=\"muted\">Finland</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;40% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 40% of days.</p><p>The forecast did only slightly better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.18</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>109&ndash;182\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>757 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Turku &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Turku\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.629333333333335,378.76444444444445 84.42535211267605,330.7323943661972 139.42000000000002,265.1604938271605 237.60842105263154,156.89473684210526 331.82941176470587,66.1764705882353 406.67499999999995,18.0 406.67499999999995,28.796610169491544 331.82941176470587,135.76470588235293 237.60842105263154,238.31578947368422 139.42000000000002,328.0740740740741 84.42535211267605,376.8732394366197 58.629333333333335,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"235.34214002642008\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"235.34214002642008\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.629333333333335,352.88 84.42535211267605,299.9718309859155 139.42000000000002,260.6666666666667 237.60842105263154,228.73684210526318 331.82941176470587,173.23529411764707 406.67499999999995,115.16949152542372\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 8% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 225 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.629333333333335\" cy=\"352.88\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 7%&amp;#10;It rained 23% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 71 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"84.42535211267605\" cy=\"299.9718309859155\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 23%&amp;#10;It rained 33% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 81 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"139.42000000000002\" cy=\"260.6666666666667\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 51%&amp;#10;It rained 42% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"237.60842105263154\" cy=\"228.73684210526318\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 77%&amp;#10;It rained 57% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 68 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"331.82941176470587\" cy=\"173.23529411764707\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 98%&amp;#10;It rained 73% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 236 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"406.67499999999995\" cy=\"115.16949152542372\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(40%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Turku the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.40) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-0.15).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>43%</td><td class='num'>-0.149</td><td class='num'>24.5%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'>0.184</td><td class='num'>14.6%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>45%</td><td class='num'>0.232</td><td class='num'>16.5%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>46%</td><td class='num'>0.398</td><td class='num'>10.0%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":60.45148,"lon":22.26869,"n":757,"n_cities":216,"name":"Turku","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0017777777777777779,"n":225,"obs":0.08,"sig":true},{"hi":0.14,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.07464788732394365,"n":71,"obs":0.22535211267605634,"sig":true},{"hi":0.35,"lo":0.14,"mean":0.23000000000000004,"n":81,"obs":0.3333333333333333,"sig":true},{"hi":0.67,"lo":0.35,"mean":0.5073684210526315,"n":76,"obs":0.42105263157894735,"sig":false},{"hi":0.9,"lo":0.67,"mean":0.7735294117647058,"n":68,"obs":0.5735294117647058,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.9,"mean":0.984957627118644,"n":236,"obs":0.7330508474576272,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":4.8,"provisional":false,"rank":160,"rank_hi":182.0,"rank_lo":108.975,"reliability":0.029215635339727247,"resolution":0.07109427744142044,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"turku","station":"TURKU ARTUKAINEN","timezone":"Europe/Helsinki"}